<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="6" type="enumerated">
  <item>The next equation, \(y=x^2−7\), looks a little different from the previous ones. Can you use what you’ve learned to find the coordinates of its vertex and determine if it opens up or down.</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item> What is the \(x\)-coordinate of the vertex? 
    
    <emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 0
  </item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item> What is the \(y\)-coordinate of the vertex? 
    
